# Code quality

## File size

- Every `.rs` file is at most **400 lines**, not counting `#[cfg(test)]` modules. `cargo xtask check-size` enforces it.
- When tests get big, move them to a sibling `tests.rs`:

```rust
// src/detector.rs
#[cfg(test)]
mod tests; // lives in src/detector/tests.rs
```

- Near the limit, split by responsibility into submodules. Don't compress code to fit.

## No duplication

- Before writing a helper, search `crates/stillwatch-core` and `crates/stillwatch-ipc` for an existing one.
- Share through traits or a common module. Never copy code between crates or backends. `jscpd` fails CI on clones outside tests.

## No panics, no unsafe

- No `unwrap`, `expect`, `panic!`, `todo!`, `unimplemented!`, or `dbg!` outside tests. Return errors (`thiserror` in libraries, `anyhow` in binaries).

```rust
// BAD
let cfg = toml::from_str::<Config>(&text).unwrap();
// GOOD
let cfg: Config = toml::from_str(&text).map_err(ConfigError::Parse)?;
```

- No `unsafe`. `unsafe_code` is forbidden workspace-wide.
- Never silence a lint with `#[allow]` to get around these rules.

## Docs and comments

- Every public item gets a `///` doc comment.
- Write comments only for constraints the code can't express (protocol quirks, ordering requirements, why a value is what it is). No comments narrating what the next line does.
